ganizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DonutWrecker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DonutWrecker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DonutWrecker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DonutWrecker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T13:01:16Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T13:01:58Z","body":"> > pivot_offset is set to 50, 50\n> \n> I opened MPR and ... pivot offset is (0, 0), not (50, 50) I set is to (50, 50) by myself and now it scales from center, as expected. Godot version: v4.6.dev2.official [[7864ac8](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/7864ac80192e9e91bf56176af9f04cc013b580aa)]\n\nHere's a video of it in not working in 2K:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fb97d457-29bb-48aa-b420-e69cac054f0e","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432255284/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432339270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111914#issuecomment-3432339270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111914","id":3432339270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MlVdG","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T13:20:30Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T13:30:50Z","body":"- I think it is caused by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/70646.\n\n> The new property is now serialized to scene instead of the old one.\n\nOpen MRP scene file in text editor, change pivot_offset in Godot Inspector to some non-zero value, save scene, inspect it in text editor - any pivot (relative or not) is not serialized.\nThis explains why I saw zero pivot_offset after opening MRP.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432339270/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432374671","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111914#issuecomment-3432374671","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111914","id":3432374671,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MleGP","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T13:29:45Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T13:29:45Z","body":"That's not a bug then, `pivot_offset` isn't meant to be stored and is editor-only, as per the description of the PR:\n> This PR adds a pivot_offset_ratio property, which is pivot_offset, but expressed as 0-1 range mapped on Control's size. The new property is now serialized to scene instead of the old one. pivot_offset is now a wrapper for setting absolute offset (kind of like rotation_degrees) and will correctly get loaded if previously saved in scenes. Changing Control's size will preserve the offset ratio.\n\nIt seems this is intentional, though not documented\n\nCC @KoBeWi ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432374671/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432381231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111914#issuecomment-3432381231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111914","id":3432381231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Mlfsv","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T13:31:31Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T13:31:31Z","body":"> * May be caused [Add `pivot_offset_ratio` property to Control #70646](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/70646), but it needs verification.\n\nYeah, `pivot_offset` is missing `PROPERTY_USAGE_STORAGE` flag (it was changed from `PROPERTY_USAGE_DEFAULT` to `PROPERTY_USAGE_EDITOR`-only).\n \n> > The new property is now serialized to scene instead of the old one.\n> \n> This explains why I saw pivot offset (0, 0) after opening MRP.\n\nThe PR description is outdated. It's describes initial approach, wasn't edited. It was later changed for the pivot to be actually a combined value of ratio+\"pixel\" offsets. And seems like while changing the approach the flag for `pivot_offset` was simply forgotten to be changed.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432381231/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]